    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d78-a1">

                <pb facs="0199" n="105" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg105"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 73.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Tillman to the
                            Minister of Foreign Affairs.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-04-15"><hi rendition="#italic">April 15,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: You stated to me some weeks ago in
                    a personal interview that Mr. St. John, named as arbitrator in the Santos claim
                    against Ecuador, was not objectionable. I beg now to ask that you will write me
                    that Mr. St. John is acceptable to Ecuador.</p>
                <p>It has occurred to me, and I have so informed Mr. Santos, that whatever agreement
                    may be reached or whatever question may be determined by an arbitrator, the
                    result should be made the judgment of the arbitrator selected in accordance with
                    the convention.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James D. Tillman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
